      "body": "Content disclosure status as of 2026-09-30\n\nTunnel Escape Fates Entwined content disclosure on the Steam store page lists the Mature Content descriptors the publisher flagged and the AI-assisted background images disclosure for media assets. The Steam store Mature Content section enumerates only the categories the developer flagged, and the AI disclosure confirms which storefront media assets use AI-assisted backgrounds. Regional ratings are not announced as of 2026-09-30.\n\nTunnel Escape Fates Entwined content disclosure — Mature content descriptors on the Steam store page\n\nThe Steam store Mature Content section for AppID 4285110 surfaces only the categories the publisher opted to flag during the store submission flow. The section is structured as a fixed taxonomy (Violence, Blood, Gore, Sexual Content, Nudity, Drugs, Self-Harm, and General Mature Content) and only lists the categories the developer marked, so an empty or short checklist is a deliberate publisher choice rather than missing data. SteamDB metadata for AppID 4285110 mirrors the same descriptor flags in the dated application snapshot. The descriptor row is the user-facing summary that parents and reviewers use when deciding whether the title fits the household.\n\nHow the AI-assisted background images disclosure is structured\n\nSteam exposes a separate \"AI Generated Content Disclosure\" block on the store page that asks the publisher to declare which storefront media assets use AI-assisted backgrounds. The disclosure for Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined confirms which screenshots and store-page artwork use generated backgrounds, and is paired with the Mature Content section on the same page. The disclosure row is a yes/no declaration per asset class rather than a per-image audit, and SteamDB metadata records the same declaration timestamp for AppID 4285110.\n\nRegional ratings and disclosure scope\n\nRegional ratings (PEGI, ESRB, USK, CERO, GRAC, GSRR, and the Australian Classification Board rating) are not announced as of 2026-09-30, so this page does not publish a per-region rating table. Steam assigns age recommendations for store-page search filtering but the formal regional rating is published through each region's classification body once the publisher submits the title. The descriptor and AI disclosure rows are global; the regional rating row is per locale and is not announced for this title yet. Re-check the canonical store page and the SteamDB dated snapshot after launch day for the first regional rating entry and any update to the disclosure scope.\n\nHow this page differs from the mature content reading guide\n\nThis page is the source of record for the Mature Content and AI disclosure flags published on the canonical store page for AppID 4285110. It is not a reading guide for in-game content; the developer-published description is the place to read the scene-by-scene framing of the zombie-virus escort mission. If you want the elevator pitch and the in-fiction setting, follow the internal link to the overview page rather than reading the disclosure row as a story summary."
